// IEEE-754 rounding, not real arithmetic -> V200 (assert violated).
// 0.1 + 0.2 is not 0.3 in binary floating point; the prover refutes the
// equality, so the assert fails. This is the FP analogue of "the prover
// actually says something": a model that treated floats as reals would
// wrongly prove it and stay silent.
fn main() @context(thread) {
    var x: f64 = 0.1d + 0.2d;
    assert(x == 0.3d);
}
